                answer: 'Yes, the Backdoor Roth is a legal tax planning strategy for high earners whose income exceeds the Roth IRA phase-out limits. It involves making a non-deductible contribution to a Traditional IRA and then converting that account into a Roth IRA. Keep in mind the IRS Pro-Rata rule if you have other pre-tax IRAs.'
